    // Market specific
    'ben_thanh_info1': 'Ben Thanh Market is located in the center of District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, built during the French colonial period in 1914. The market has a T-shaped architecture with two entrances, next to the old Ben Thanh roundabout, serving as a cultural icon of Saigon.',
    'ben_thanh_info2': 'Ben Thanh Market is famous for its diverse products: fresh produce, fabrics, shoes, souvenirs, and especially street food. The bustling atmosphere, commercial vibe, and diverse cultural exchange create its unique character.',
    'ben_thanh_info3': 'The market preserves memories of many generations of merchants and Saigon residents. To preserve it, we need to collect old photos, take current photos, digitize maps, and interview merchants to recreate the market\'s changes over time.',

    // Ben Thanh Market detailed content
    'ben_thanh_general_info': 'Ben Thanh Market is located in the old District 1 center, now in Ben Thanh Ward, Ho Chi Minh City. It is one of the city\'s most famous markets, notable for its clock tower at the main entrance and diverse trading activities.',
    'ben_thanh_origin': 'The market\'s name is associated with its location near the old Ben Nghe river wharf, where locals and visitors often docked to enter Gia Dinh City.',
    'ben_thanh_milestone_1': 'Pre-French colonial period',
    'ben_thanh_milestone_1_desc': 'The market originated from a riverside market before the French colonial period.',
    'ben_thanh_milestone_2': 'Late 19th century',
    'ben_thanh_milestone_2_desc': 'The old market deteriorated and needed rebuilding.',
    'ben_thanh_milestone_3': '1914',
    'ben_thanh_milestone_3_desc': 'The new market was built at its current location and inaugurated.',
    'ben_thanh_architecture': 'Ben Thanh Market has a T-shaped architecture with two main entrances. Notable for its clock tower at the main entrance, the market is a cultural icon of Saigon\'s commerce.',
    'ben_thanh_characteristics_1': 'The market is famous for its diverse products: fresh produce, fabrics, shoes, souvenirs, and especially street food.',
    'ben_thanh_characteristics_2': 'The bustling commercial atmosphere and diverse cultural exchange create the market\'s unique character.',
    'ben_thanh_heritage_1': 'The market preserves memories of many generations of merchants and Saigon residents.',
    'ben_thanh_heritage_2': 'To preserve it, we need to collect old photos, take current photos, digitize maps, and interview merchants to recreate the market\'s changes over time.',
    
    'tan_dinh_info1': 'Tan Dinh Market is located on Hai Ba Trung Street, Ho Chi Minh City, formerly Phu Hoa Market, formed around the 1870s-1880s. It was rebuilt in 1926 and inaugurated on July 26, 1927. In 2025, the market was recognized as a city-level architectural and artistic monument.',
    'tan_dinh_info2': 'The market features French architecture with three front towers and Art Deco style. It is famous for fabrics, fresh produce, and local cuisine. The close trading atmosphere between merchants and regular customers helps preserve traditional Saigon market culture.',
    'tan_dinh_info3': 'The market preserves memories of many generations through fabric stalls, shops, and long-standing trading professions. To preserve it, we need to collect old photos, take current photos, digitize maps, and interview merchants to recreate the market\'s changes over time.',
    
    'ba_chieu_info1': 'Ba Chieu Market is located in the Phan Dang Luu – Le Quang Dinh area, Binh Thanh District, Ho Chi Minh City. Formed in the 19th century, it was originally called Xom Market. According to writer Son Nam, the name Ba Chieu is associated with a goddess worshipped beside a natural pond. Rebuilt in 1942 and upgraded in 1987, from the old Gia Dinh trading center, it still serves local life today.',
    'ba_chieu_info2': 'The market developed from a traditional gathering place into a market complex with diverse products. The surrounding area is famous for affordable clothing, shoes, and night trading. Direct trading atmosphere and the closeness between buyers and sellers create its unique character.',
    'ba_chieu_info3': 'The market preserves memories of long-standing merchants and many generations of residents. Collecting old photos, taking current photos, saving maps, videos, and interviews helps compare the market\'s past and present, contributing to preserving Gia Dinh\'s history and traditional market culture.',
    
    'an_dong_info1': 'An Dong Market is on An Duong Vuong Street, in the Cholon area, Ho Chi Minh City. Formed around 1950-1954, it is associated with the Chinese community\'s trading activities. The old market was built in 1954; construction of the new market began in 1989 and opened in 1991. Today, it is a famous fashion trading hub.',
    'an_dong_info2': 'The market developed into a multi-story commercial complex with thousands of stalls, specializing in clothing, fabrics, shoes, and accessories. Wholesale trading, business acumen, and the Chinese community\'s influence create its unique character.',
    'an_dong_info3': 'The market is a livelihood for many business households, preserving memories of many generations of merchants. Today, trading activities are affected by purchasing power and online shopping trends. Collecting old photos, taking current photos, saving maps, videos, and interviewing merchants helps record changes, contributing to preserving Cholon\'s commercial history.',

    // Tan Dinh Market detailed content
