    // Gieo Que Quiz Translations
    'gieo_que_fact_1': 'Vietnamese banh mi originated from French baguette, but has become a completely different dish. Baguette was introduced to Vietnam during the French colonial period. Vietnamese people transformed the bread with light interior, crispy crust, pate, cold cuts, herbs, pickles, and sauce. Notably, the word "banh mi" was added to the Oxford English Dictionary in 2011.',
    'gieo_que_fact_2': 'Com tam is a symbolic dish of Saigon. Tam is broken rice, small uneven grains often discarded. Vietnamese people creatively cooked tam into com tam, eaten with grilled ribs, cha, bi, eggs, cucumber, pickles. The word "com tam" was also added to the Oxford English Dictionary in 2022.',
    'gieo_que_fact_3': 'Nam Vang hu tieu is associated with Cambodia but has become a Vietnamese creation. There are two main types: hu tieu nam (clear, fresh broth) and hu tieu kho (no broth, eaten with soy sauce). Southern people prefer hu tieu nam, Northern people prefer hu tieu kho.',
    'gieo_que_fact_4': 'Banh xeo originated from Central Vietnam, especially Binh Dinh and Quang Ngai. Cake is made from rice flour, grilled on cast iron skillet until golden crispy. Eaten with fresh herbs, shrimp, meat, fish sauce mixed with lemon chili. Today banh xeo has many variations like Western banh xeo, Hue banh xeo.',
    'gieo_que_fact_5': 'Bun dau mam tom is a famous Hanoi street food. Mam tom is made from fresh shrimp, fermented 3-6 months. Dish includes bun, fried tofu, pork, floss, mam tom, herbs. Usually eaten with spicy garlic vinegar.',
    'gieo_que_fact_6': 'Pha lau originated from Chinese people in Saigon. Main ingredients are animal offal (heart, liver, phèo, intestines) cooked with sugar, fish sauce, vinegar, star anise, cinnamon. Pha lau usually eaten with rice, banh mi, or hu tieu.',
    'gieo_que_fact_7': 'Xoi is a traditional Vietnamese breakfast dish with thousands of years of history. Xoi gac (chicken xoi) is the most popular type, made from glutinous rice, mung bean filling, chicken meat, black glutinous rice. Savory xoi, sweet xoi, egg xoi, rubbed xoi... each type has unique flavor.',
    'gieo_que_fact_8': 'Bot chien is a street food influenced by Chinese cuisine. Batter made from rice flour, glutinous rice flour, chicken egg, coconut milk, fried on hot skillet. Bot chien usually eaten with sweet cucumber, sweet and sour fish sauce.',
    'gieo_que_fact_9': 'Bo bia originated from China but completely Vietnamized. Ingredients include pork skin, pork ear, boiled meat, quail eggs, fresh herbs, cucumber, pickles, wrapped in rice paper. Name "bo bia" means "buffalo cow" in Cantonese.',
    'gieo_que_fact_10': 'Che is a traditional Vietnamese dessert with hundreds of types. Thai che, tapioca che, lotus seed longan che, banana river seed che, purple potato che... Each region has distinctive che. Che is not only delicious but also has cooling and beautifying effects.',
    'gieo_que_quiz_1_question': 'What ingredients does Saigon banh mi typically combine with?',
    'gieo_que_quiz_1_option_a': 'A. Pate, cold cuts, herbs, and pickles',
    'gieo_que_quiz_1_option_b': 'B. Blue cheese and Italian pasta',
    'gieo_que_quiz_1_option_c': 'C. Kimchi and seaweed',
    'gieo_que_quiz_1_option_d': 'D. Peanut butter and fruit jam',
    'gieo_que_quiz_1_answer': 'A',
    'gieo_que_quiz_1_explanation': 'Saigon banh mi typically combines pate, cold cuts, herbs, cucumber, and pickles.',
    'gieo_que_quiz_2_question': 'Which street food dish usually consists of pieces of rice flour fried with eggs?',
    'gieo_que_quiz_2_option_a': 'A. Banh khuot',
    'gieo_que_quiz_2_option_b': 'B. Bot chien',
    'gieo_que_quiz_2_option_c': 'C. Banh cuon',
    'gieo_que_quiz_2_option_d': 'D. Banh beo',
    'gieo_que_quiz_2_answer': 'B',
    'gieo_que_quiz_2_explanation': 'Bot chien is a popular dish with Chinese culinary influence in Saigon.',
    'gieo_que_quiz_3_question': 'Pha lau is mainly prepared from which ingredient?',
    'gieo_que_quiz_3_option_a': 'A. Various types of beans',
    'gieo_que_quiz_3_option_b': 'B. Fresh seafood',
    'gieo_que_quiz_3_option_c': 'C. Animal offal',
    'gieo_que_quiz_3_option_d': 'D. Tropical fruits',
    'gieo_que_quiz_3_answer': 'C',
    'gieo_que_quiz_3_explanation': 'Pha lau mainly uses offal, cooked with various fragrant spices.',
    'gieo_que_quiz_4_question': 'Nam Vang hu tieu is associated with which city in Cambodia?',
    'gieo_que_quiz_4_option_a': 'A. Siem Reap',
    'gieo_que_quiz_4_option_b': 'B. Phnom Penh',
    'gieo_que_quiz_4_option_c': 'C. Battambang',
    'gieo_que_quiz_4_option_d': 'D. Sihanoukville',
    'gieo_que_quiz_4_answer': 'B',
    'gieo_que_quiz_4_explanation': 'Nam Vang is the Sino-Vietnamese name associated with Phnom Penh, the capital of Cambodia.',
    'gieo_que_quiz_5_question': 'What clearly demonstrates cultural fusion in Ho Chi Minh City cuisine?',
    'gieo_que_quiz_5_option_a': 'A. All dishes have the same origin',
    'gieo_que_quiz_5_option_b': 'B. Only using imported ingredients',
    'gieo_que_quiz_5_option_c': 'C. Many dishes combine Vietnamese, Chinese, and other culinary influences',
    'gieo_que_quiz_5_option_d': 'D. Cuisine only has traditional dishes',
    'gieo_que_quiz_5_answer': 'C',
    'gieo_que_quiz_5_explanation': 'Ho Chi Minh City cuisine formed through exchange, reception, and adaptation between many communities.',
